1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,041
What if everyone could see your thoughts?

2
00:00:03,081 --> 00:00:06,355
You step outside, and every head wears a bubble.

3
00:00:06,395 --> 00:00:06,769
Pizza.

4
00:00:06,809 --> 00:00:07,528
Late again.

5
00:00:07,568 --> 00:00:08,150
Cute dog.

6
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:10,014
And yours, in huge letters:

7
00:00:10,054 --> 00:00:11,671
why is everyone staring?

8
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,161
On a first date,

9
00:00:13,201 --> 00:00:14,737
things get awkward fast.

10
00:00:14,777 --> 00:00:16,510
He thinks she is wonderful.

11
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,612
She thinks, don't spill the tea.

12
00:00:18,652 --> 00:00:19,860
Both blush at once,

13
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:22,947
which is the most honest first date in history.

14
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,511
At work, Monday morning becomes a thriller.

15
00:00:27,551 --> 00:00:29,583
The boss thinks, I hate meetings.

16
00:00:29,623 --> 00:00:31,153
Karen thinks, free lunch?

17
00:00:31,193 --> 00:00:32,661
And Dave's bubble reads:

18
00:00:32,701 --> 00:00:33,603
updating my CV.

19
00:00:33,643 --> 00:00:35,173
Somebody coughs politely.

20
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:36,832
Exams are tricky too.

21
00:00:36,872 --> 00:00:38,752
A student wonders about answer B,

22
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:40,788
and the teacher reads it instantly.

23
00:00:40,828 --> 00:00:44,861
Cheating is impossible, but strangely everyone's handwriting improves.

24
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:46,690
Poker night is chaos.

25
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:49,450
Nobody can bluff when their thoughts read,

26
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:50,632
I have two sevens.

27
00:00:50,672 --> 00:00:54,969
The game collapses into a very friendly conversation about snacks.

28
00:00:55,450 --> 00:00:57,849
Try not to think about a pink elephant,

29
00:00:57,889 --> 00:01:00,601
and suddenly the entire town is wearing pink

30
00:01:00,641 --> 00:01:02,353
elephants above their heads.

31
00:01:02,393 --> 00:01:04,979
Trying not to think about something is the

32
00:01:05,019 --> 00:01:06,418
loudest thought of all.

33
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:09,150
Here's the twist.

34
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:11,657
Once everyone sees each other's thoughts,

35
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:13,492
they discover the same secret.

36
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:15,266
Everyone is nervous, hopeful,

37
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:17,345
and secretly hoping you like them.

38
00:01:17,385 --> 00:01:18,874
Almost nobody is judging.

39
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:22,050
So the whole town gathers in the square

40
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:23,525
for one enormous hug.

41
00:01:23,565 --> 00:01:26,054
A thousand bubbles float above them,

42
00:01:26,094 --> 00:01:29,004
and every single one shows the same shape:

43
00:01:29,044 --> 00:01:30,339
a small, shy heart.
